## PRE-EXISTING defect found while verifying (NOT introduced by NEARS-3749)
The script's header asserts 'Laravel app.timezone=UTC, so Monolog writes UTC timestamps' and
compares log timestamps against a UTC-computed window boundary as fixed-width strings.
Observed runtime: config('app.timezone')=UTC BUT date_default_timezone_get()=Asia/Dubai, and the
log files carry local +04:00 stamps:
"timestamp":"2026-09-25T00:56:42.986679+04:00"
  laravel.log form: [2026-09-24 18:30:14]
  UTC at that moment was 4h earlier. The window filter therefore treats lines as 'recent' for up to
  ~4h past the intended window -> biases toward stale/false alerts, NOT toward missed ones.
  Window/TZ logic was untouched by this ticket (diff covers only MATCH + payload text + header).
